---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';

const description =
  'How Dastan Aitzhanov came to work across software, cloud platforms, and investing, and what he is thinking about now.';
---

<Base title="About" description={description}>
  <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      I build software, and I allocate capital. They have never felt like separate kinds of work.
    </p>
    <p>
      The technical thread runs through cloud infrastructure, data platforms, and machine learning.
      I worked at Amazon Web Services and at Databricks. The problems I liked were practical ones:
      getting data to a place a model could use, making a system reliable enough that someone would
      trust it on an ordinary day, and finding which part of a stack was actually doing the work.
    </p>
    <p>
      Alongside that, I have spent about a decade investing personal and family capital. Real estate,
      hotels, multifamily housing, private businesses, public equities, technology, alternatives.
      Owning something changes the way a spreadsheet reads. You start to care about operations,
      incentives, and what is left after the model is right.
    </p>
    <p>
      What I am working through now is the overlap. How AI systems — agents, models that run near
      the person using them, the machinery of context and routing — change knowledge work, personal
      computing, and the design of organizations. I write about that here when a thought is ready.
      Current experiments stay off the projects page until there is something definite to show.
    </p>
    <p>I live in Texas.</p>
    <p>
      Email is the way to reach me:
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      Code I have published lives on <a href={site.github} rel="me">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
